<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Amritsar (1809)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1809</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Amritsar of 1809 was an agreement between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a> and the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>. It fixed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutlej-river">Sutlej River</a> as the boundary between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> and British spheres of influence. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> profile notes that this settlement secured Ranjit Singh's eastern flank and gave him room to expand his empire westwards and northwards.</p></div>
